The code needs to be adapted to the specifics of the codebase where it is to be used. The OLD(...) syntax is to indicate "the value of variable 'variable_name' IMMEDIATELY BEFORE the operation" while "RET" stands for "return value" of the function (i.e., the 'x' in "return x;"). The comments starting with @@@ are to be translated into assert statements that check whether the code behaves as it should according to the comment.--------------------
